HST Office: ribbon UX engine — groups reopen into free room, ribbon-only labels and two-line tooltips,
one banner width per app, captions on one line, contextual tabs marked and opened after an insert.

From the ribbon UX audit of 13/11/2026 (plans/reports/fable52-261113-1224-ribbon-ux-audit.md, section 2):
- PriorityMergedHBox: select() stops at the first ladder step that fits, and that step can free far more
  than was missing; every tab now grows its groups back into that room, most used first (the reverse of
  the tab's fold order, left to right without a ladder of its own), collapsed groups before shrunk ones
  (vcl/inc/HstRibbonRegrow.hxx, unit tested by tests/unit/test_ribbon_regrow.py). A 1920 px window no
  longer shows a "Caption ▾" group button beside free room.
- VclBuilder: "hst-ribbon-label" (translatable) names a toolbox item on the ribbon only, so the ribbon can
  use short, familiar terms while menus and the feature search keep the command label; and
  "hst-ribbon-description" (translatable) adds a second tooltip line saying what the command does.
- NotebookbarTabControl: the wide banner narrows for the widest tab page measured so far instead of the
  current page, so it keeps one width while the user switches tabs (still 260-360 px, ratio kept).
- PriorityMergedHBox takes the full height of its tab and VclGrid drops a ribbon group's caption to the
  bottom of the room it gets: the captions of every group and every tab stand on one line.
- Tab control: a contextual tab (its page is not shown in every context) has its label in the accent
  colour under a thin accent band; a selection made right after an insert command (picture, table,
  chart, shape...; reported by the sfx dispatcher) opens its contextual tab, while clicking an existing
  object still leaves the ribbon on the current tab.
- The feature search box shows a one-time hint the first time it appears in a profile ("Không thấy lệnh? Gõ
  tên lệnh ở đây, không cần dấu."); it closes at the first search or after 12 s (BubbleShown in the
  extension's FeatureSearch configuration, search.xcs).

